---
import AdminNav from '../../components/AdminNav.astro';
import DfsSpend from '../../components/DfsSpend.astro';
import '@fontsource/sora/400.css';
import '@fontsource/sora/600.css';
import '../../styles/website-audit.css';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"/><title>Website Audit | NC Digital Admin</title></head><body>
<AdminNav />
<DfsSpend />
<header class="topbar"><a href="/admin/links/" class="brand">Website Audit</a></header>
<main><section class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">WEBSITE AUDIT & SALES REPORT</p><h1>See what needs work.<br/><span>Show what you can improve.</span></h1><p>A focused website check with page-level evidence and a branded report you can take to your next client conversation.</p></div><div class="cost"><strong>~5p</strong><span>per audit with local rankings<br/>free without them</span></div></section>
<section class="panel start"><form id="audit-form"><fieldset id="audit-fields"><div class="form-grid"><label>Website address<input id="website" required maxlength="500" placeholder="https://example.co.uk" autocomplete="url"/></label><label>Client / business name<input id="client" maxlength="120" placeholder="Optional"/></label><label>Main service <span class="hint">for local rankings · optional</span><input id="service" maxlength="80" placeholder="e.g. roofer"/></label><label>Town <span class="hint">optional</span><input id="town" list="audit-towns" maxlength="150" placeholder="e.g. Cardiff" autocomplete="off"/><datalist id="audit-towns"></datalist></label><label>Audit size<select id="page-limit"><option value="10">Up to 10 pages</option><option value="5">Quick check · 5 pages</option></select></label><button class="primary" id="start" type="submit" disabled>Audit website ↗</button></div><div class="form-foot"><p>Checks key pages and up to 20 further internal links. Add a service and town to include local Google rankings (about 5–6p of DataForSEO credit). Saved reports are reused for 7 days.</p><label class="checkbox"><input id="refresh" type="checkbox"/> Run a fresh audit</label></div></fieldset></form></section>
<div class="history"><label for="history">Saved audits</label><select id="history"><option value="">Choose a report…</option></select><button id="open-report">Open report</button></div>
<div id="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>
<section id="progress" class="panel progress" hidden><div><p class="eyebrow">AUDIT PROGRESS</p><h2 id="phase"></h2><div class="progress-meter"><div class="progress-track" id="progress-bar" role="progressbar" aria-label="Audit progress" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="0"><i id="progress-fill"></i></div><strong id="progress-pct">0%</strong></div><p id="progress-copy"></p></div><div class="actions"><button id="resume" hidden>Resume audit</button><button id="stop">Stop audit</button></div></section>
<section id="empty" class="empty"><div class="empty-mark">↗</div><h2>Useful evidence for a better sales conversation.</h2><div class="features"><div><span>01</span><h3>Check the foundations</h3><p>Find missing SEO essentials, mobile setup issues and broken internal links.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Explain the opportunity</h3><p>See what was found, why it matters and a practical fix for each finding.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Make it client-ready</h3><p>Add your recommendations and save an NC Digital report as a PDF or standalone document.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="results" hidden>
<div class="report-tools"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR AUDIT</p><h2 id="report-title"></h2><p id="report-spend" class="spend" hidden></p></div><div class="actions"><button id="rerun" title="Re-runs every check into this report. The client link stays the same.">Update with fresh data</button><button id="email-open" class="primary">Email to client</button><button id="share">Create client link</button><button id="download">Download report</button><button class="primary" id="print">Print / save PDF</button></div></div>
<section id="email-panel" class="panel email-panel" hidden><div class="email-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">EMAIL THE REVIEW</p><p class="share-help">Sent from nathan@nc-digital.co.uk through the CRM with your usual sign-off and signature. Their reply lands in your CRM inbox, and a follow-up task is added for 3 days’ time.</p></div><button id="email-close" type="button" aria-label="Close">✕</button></div><form id="email-form"><div class="email-grid"><label>Contact name<input id="email-name" maxlength="120" placeholder="e.g. Gareth Evans" autocomplete="off"/></label><label>Email address<input id="email-to" type="email" required maxlength="254" placeholder="name@business.co.uk" autocomplete="off"/></label></div><p class="email-subject"><strong>Subject:</strong> Your website review from NC Digital [reference added automatically]</p><label>Message <span class="hint">written from this report; edit it as you like</span><textarea id="email-message" rows="14" maxlength="8000" required></textarea></label><div class="email-actions"><button class="primary" id="email-send" type="submit">Send email</button><button id="email-rewrite" type="button">Rewrite from report</button><span id="email-status" role="status"></span></div></form><div id="email-history" class="email-history"></div></section>
<section id="share-panel" class="panel share-panel" hidden><div><p class="eyebrow">CLIENT LINK</p><p class="share-help">Send this link to the client. It shows the client report only, never your notes panel or spend. You get an email when they open it; your own previews from here don’t count.</p></div><div class="share-row"><input id="share-url" readonly aria-label="Client report link"/><button id="copy-share" type="button">Copy link</button><a id="open-share" class="button" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open ↗</a><button id="unshare" type="button">Turn off link</button></div><p id="share-stats" class="share-stats"></p></section>
<details class="panel editor" id="editor"><summary>Personalise the client report</summary><form id="notes-form"><label>Client / business name<input id="report-client" maxlength="120" required/></label><label>Your introduction<textarea id="summary" maxlength="4000" rows="3" placeholder="What matters most for this business?"></textarea></label><label>What to offer <select id="offer"><option value="auto">Automatic: SEO if they use WordPress, otherwise a new WordPress website</option><option value="website">A new WordPress website</option><option value="seo">Local SEO &amp; Google ranking</option><option value="none">Don’t show an offer</option></select></label><label>Recommended work / next steps<textarea id="notes" maxlength="6000" rows="5" placeholder="Add your proposed scope, priorities and next step for the client."></textarea></label><button type="submit">Save report notes</button><span id="notes-status" role="status"></span></form></details>
<div id="report-document"></div>
<details class="panel editor internal" id="internal"><summary>Your notes: technical detail, <span id="internal-count">0</span> items to check (not in the client report)</summary><div id="internal-body"></div></details>
</section>
</main><script>import '../../scripts/website-audit.js';</script></body></html>
